<template v-if="slug==='manifest'"><section class="pg-card"><h2>Theme playground</h2><p>These preview controls illustrate manifest values. In applications, use <code>defineVirexenUI()</code> to supply defaults.</p><div class="pg-cols"><label>Theme preset<select v-model="preset"><option value="default">Default · Virexen teal</option><option value="calm">Calm · Soft surfaces</option><option value="bold">Bold · High emphasis</option><option value="enterprise">Enterprise · Refined neutrals</option></select></label><label>Appearance<select v-model="appearance"><option value="system">System</option><option value="light">Light</option><option value="dark">Dark</option></select></label></div><div class="pg-preview"><span class="pg-swatch"></span><strong>{{preset}} theme</strong><span>Appearance: {{appearance}}</span></div><h3>Manifest example</h3><pre>{{`export default defineVirexenUI({\n  app: { id: 'demo', name: 'Demo' },\n  theme: { preset: '${preset}', appearance: '${appearance}' },\n  localization: { defaultLanguage: 'en-GB', defaultCountry: 'GB' }\n});`}}</pre><p class="pg-help">This page demonstrates configuration values. It does not change your app's installed manifest or persist preferences.</p></section></template>
